            "description": "Watch Deportes Tolima vs Coquimbo Unido highlights and goals from CONMEBOL Libertadores on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on April 29, 2026. High-stakes continental football took center stage on April 29, 2026, as Deportes Tolima hosted Coquimbo Unido in a gripping CONMEBOL Libertadores encounter. Both sides looked to assert their dominance in a match defined by tactical shifts and intense individual battles under the lights. A Cagey Opening Exchange The match began with both teams searching for a rhythm, but the early proceedings were marked more by physical challenges than fluid attacking play. On April 29, 2026, the competitive nature of the CONMEBOL Libertadores was on full display as the referee was forced to go to his pocket early. In the 18th minute, a heated confrontation resulted in yellow cards for both Cristian Arrieta and Cristian Zavala , setting a combative tone for the remainder of the first half. Despite several half-chances, neither side could find the clinical edge required to break the deadlock before the interval, leading to a scoreless stalemate at the break. Second Half Fireworks and the Penalty Breakthrough The tactical chess match evolved rapidly after the restart as the intensity shifted up a gear. In the 59th minute, the deadlock was finally broken when Deportes Tolima were awarded a penalty following a foul by Manuel Fernandez , who received a yellow card for his troubles. Sebastian Guzman stepped up to the spot and showing nerves of steel, powered his effort home to give the home side the lead. However, the celebrations were short-lived as Coquimbo Unido refused to buckle under the pressure. Just seven minutes after falling behind, the Chilean visitors found their response. A well-orchestrated move saw Juan Pablo Torres provide a precise assist for Luis Sandoval , who finished clinicaly in the 66th minute to restore parity. The equalizer prompted a flurry of tactical changes from both benches, with Coquimbo Unido introducing veteran presence in Lucas Pratto , while Tolima looked for fresh legs in the final third. Jersson Gonzalez Decides the Contest The managerial gamble from the Deportes Tolima dugout proved to be the masterstroke of the evening. In the 70th minute, Jersson Gonzalez was introduced to the fray, and it took him only eight minutes to make a defining impact on the match. In the 78th minute, Gonzalez found space in the box and fired home to put the hosts back in front, sparking wild celebrations in the stands. As the clock ticked toward the final whistle, Coquimbo Unido pushed for a second equalizer, but their frustrations grew as Guido Vadala was cautioned in the 84th minute. Tolima managed the closing stages with composure, navigating six minutes of stoppage time to secure all three points. The referee’s final whistle confirmed a hard-fought victory for the Colombian side, leaving the visitors to rue their missed opportunities in a pulsating second half.",
